    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i run a small online stationery shop in lyon and we have our quarterly audit coming up soon. i need to make sure we are actually following gdpr rules properly. can u just give me a summary of the main principles we need to care about since we mostly just collect customer emails and shipping addresses for orders?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As GDPR applies to your online shop, the main principles to focus on are: (1) Lawfulness, where data processing is based on explicit consent from customers for collecting and storing their personal data, and (2) Data Protection by design and by default, meaning you need to implement measures that securely store and process customer data. You should also ensure Data Minimisation, only collecting the data necessary for your business operations. (3) Data Accuracy, keeping customer records up-to-date, and (4) Right to Erasure, allowing customers to delete their data upon request.",
